# SEC-001: the build context must never carry secrets, data, or local state.
# Deny broadly first, then re-include only the runtime source tree. Both the
# directory and its descendants must be negated: re-including a directory does
# not automatically re-include children that were excluded by `*`.
*

# --- runtime source (allowlist) ---
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!server.js
!db.js
!routes/
!routes/**
!lib/
!lib/**
!views/
!views/**
!public/
!public/**
!data/
!data/**
!migrations/
!migrations/**
!scripts/
!scripts/**

# --- re-deny anything sensitive that the allowlist above would otherwise pull in ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
data/master.key
data/backups/
data/email-dev-outbox.log
uploads/
backups/
.demo-backup/
output/
tmp/
node_modules/
.git/
.github/
tests/
**/*.log
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.enc
.DS_Store
